---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: The spike-brief writer's task of a plan's spikes run.
variables:
  plan:
    description: The qualified id of the plan whose spikes are briefed.
    type: text
    required: true
  native:
    description: The plan project's native id.
    type: text
    required: true
---
Read the spike tasks of `{{ plan }}-spikes` and the draft plan `{{ plan }}`, and write the
spike brief the manager relays while the spikes run beside you: exactly one document of
`{{ plan }}` with the native id `{{ native }}-spike-brief`, rendered from the `spike-brief`
template as `onepipeline template resolve spike-brief --json` resolves it, with one entry per
spike task, by its node id.

Once that document is written, raise exactly one non-blocking `check-in` surface on your own
run, its text on standard input and never through `--message`:

```sh
scripts/onepipeline.sh surface --kind check-in "$ONEPIPELINE_RUN_ID" <<'BRIEF'
Spike brief {{ native }}-spike-brief of {{ plan }}:
- <spike node id>: <what it measures, in a few words>
BRIEF
```

Its first line names the document `{{ native }}-spike-brief` and `{{ plan }}`; then one line
per spike task of `{{ plan }}-spikes`, its node id and, in a few words, what it measures. This
text is what the manager relays to the user, who may redirect a spike while it runs. Raise
no human item and ask nothing blocking: nothing waits on this brief.

## Acceptance criteria

- `{{ plan }}` holds the document `{{ native }}-spike-brief`, rendered from the `spike-brief` template, with one question and use for each spike task of `{{ plan }}-spikes` and no other.
- After writing it, this dispatch raised exactly one non-blocking `check-in` surface on its own run, its text on standard input, naming `{{ native }}-spike-brief` and `{{ plan }}` and giving one line per spike task of `{{ plan }}-spikes` — its node id and what it measures — and raised no human item or blocking question.

## Additional info

This dispatch writes only to the plan store, which is gitignored, and to its own run's
channel: it commits nothing and leaves the checkout on its base branch.
